Description: Sync src/load_ams.cpp with upstream master
 Fedora builds the 0.8.9.0 tarball from 2017, which predates all of the AMS
 loader hardening upstream did in 2021. This brings src/load_ams.cpp up to
 the current upstream state so the CVE-2026-111271 fix applies on top of it
 rather than beside it.
 .
 Upstream commits, oldest first:
 .
   1bef4e1  Add bounds checks to Extreme's Tracker AMS loader.
   11871de  Fix Velvet Studio AMS crash, constify pointers.
   31910e1  Fix another Extreme's AMS crash.
   ecf8df0  Fix AMS slow loads due to large garbage samples.
   6948105  Fix AMS2 instrument bounding checks.
   4282f68  Add more missing consts in AMS loaders.
   5e1443f  Add missing AMSUnpack bounds checks.
   cd6baf2  Shrink AMS samples if the packed size can't possibly fit them.
   70d73b9  Fix off-by-one AMS pattern bounds checks.
   f768b60  Add extra AMS2 pitchenv bounds check in case support is ever added.
   63133e8  multiple warning fixes and build updates (load_ams.cpp part only)
 .
 The backport is self contained: MAX_SAMPLE_LENGTH is already defined in
 0.8.9.0's sndfile.h, ReadSample() already takes LPCSTR there, and the new
 AMSUnpackCheck() is file local. No header changes are needed.
 .
 Note that none of this touches the ReadAMS2() pattern decoder. 70d73b9 added
 exactly this class of bound to the ReadAMS() v1 decoder and the v2 decoder
 was left alone; that is what CVE-2026-111271 is about, fixed separately.
